Image caption generator:

Schematic diagram of image caption generator



An image is first processed by a pre-trained VGG model to extract a 4096-feature vector, which is reduced to 256 dimensions.
A sequence of words is processed using an embedding layer and an LSTM to also produce a 256-dimensional vector.
These two vectors are combined (added) and passed through dense layers to predict the next word in the sentence using a softmax output over the vocabulary.

The metrics these models are tested on:
BLEU-1: 0.579114
BLEU-2: 0.344856  <main metrics>
BLEU-3: 0.252154
BLEU-4: 0.131446



Almost everything we need to generate captions for entirely new photographs is in the model file.To reuse we need the Tokenizer for encoding generated words for the model while generating a sequence, and the maximum length of input sequences, used when we defined the model (e.g. 34).

